# tools/morphology_gradient_witness.rish -- the morphological gradient proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the DETECT verb of the nonlinear morphology floor, the first derived operation
# standing on image/morphology.rye's dilate (max) and erode (min). Where the convolution floor's detect verb is edges.rye
# (the Sobel gradient of a weighted sum), this is the gradient of a RANK filter: dilate grows a bright mark and erode
# shrinks it, so the two disagree exactly at a TRANSITION and agree on any flat region, and their difference
# `dilate(x) - erode(x)` is the THICKNESS of the boundary at each pixel -- zero on a flat interior or exterior, bright at
# every edge, measured with no float and no square root, just a subtraction. The outline, mask border, and contour a
# surface reaches for the day it wants a shape's edge.
#
# One subtraction, three operand pairs -- the crux this witness proves is the ADDITIVE LAW: the full gradient decomposes
# exactly into the OUTER ring `dilate - src` (just outside a shape) plus the INNER ring `src - erode` (the shape's own
# edge), two disjoint halves of the one boundary whose sum is the full gradient byte-for-byte. Because dilate is a max over
# a window that includes the center and erode a min over the same, extensivity gives `dilate >= src >= erode` everywhere,
# so no subtraction can underflow a byte and the ring sum never saturates. On metal: radius 0 is the degenerate blank
# gradient; the gradient equals dilate - erode byte-for-byte through morphology's own verbs (the definition crux); a
# boundary lights to 255 while both flat regions stay dark; the two rings are disjoint and one-sided; a flat field is
# blank; alpha is measured like any channel; the result round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte; an over-max
# radius and an empty source refuse by name; the same gradient is deterministic. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/morphology_gradient_witness.rish

say "morphology_gradient: Language EN -- Season G morphology gradient; an RGBA image's boundaries lit by dilate (max) minus erode (min) over a square structuring element, the detect verb of the nonlinear morphology floor."
say "morphology_gradient: Style Radiant -- one subtraction over three operand pairs; the full gradient (dilate - erode) is the sum of an outer ring (dilate - src) and an inner ring (src - erode), two disjoint halves of the one boundary, extensivity keeping every difference a real byte."
say "morphology_gradient: Lens TAME -- u32 in-memory counts, the radius bounded and refused by name through morphology's own guard; each function states its invariants positively; the source and radius guarded once before any allocation so a refusal allocates nothing; the subtraction asserts high >= low (extensivity) at every byte, so no channel can underflow; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/morphology_gradient"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/morphology_gradient.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "morphology_gradient: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "morphology_gradient: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "morphology_gradient: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-morphology-gradient" else "morphology_gradient: selftest did not print the GREEN line"

say "morphology_gradient: GREEN -- the morphological gradient lights an RGBA image's boundaries, equal to dilate minus erode byte-for-byte, the outer and inner rings summing to the full gradient with no saturation, on metal."
